<!DOCTYPE template>
<!--
  One deck's strip: what the FLX6 cannot show. Deck badge, key, BPM, title and
  artist, elapsed time, the summary overview, the chip that opens the cue
  drawer on this deck, and the two-tap eject chip beside it.

  That eject chip is the only deck eject on the appliance. The FLX6 binds
  eject on a sampler pad's shift-press and nowhere else, so until it existed a
  loaded deck could only be cleared by loading over it or restarting the app.

  The whole strip is bound to track_loaded, so an empty deck takes no width.
  Four loaded decks give each strip ~320px of the 1280; two give each ~640.
  That collapse is also why there is no eject-reset here: deck.xml needed a
  static 0:00.00 layer because WNumberPos keeps the last position after an
  eject, and a strip that is hidden when unloaded cannot show a stale time.

  Cut from deck.xml deliberately: the track number and the rate-range block.
  At 320px per strip they do not earn the space, and the tempo is on the
  controller's own display.

  Variables:
    channel: deck number, 1 to 4.
-->
<Template>
  <WidgetGroup>
    <ObjectName>DeckStrip</ObjectName>
    <Layout>vertical</Layout>
    <SizePolicy>me,max</SizePolicy>
    <Children>

      <WidgetGroup>
        <ObjectName>DeckStripHeader</ObjectName>
        <Layout>horizontal</Layout>
        <Size>0me,24f</Size>
        <Children>
          <Label>
            <ObjectName>DeckStripBadge</ObjectName>
            <Text>DECK<Variable name="channel"/></Text>
            <Size>52f,24f</Size>
            <Connection>
              <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],play</ConfigKey>
              <BindProperty>highlight</BindProperty>
            </Connection>
            <!-- Sync leader: 0 off, 1 soft, 2 explicit. Plain SYNC can promote a
                 deck to soft leader too, so this is real leader state, not a button. -->
            <Connection>
              <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],sync_leader</ConfigKey>
              <BindProperty>master</BindProperty>
            </Connection>
          </Label>
          <Key>
            <ObjectName>DeckStripKey</ObjectName>
            <TooltipId>visual_key</TooltipId>
            <Size>44max,24f</Size>
            <Alignment>center</Alignment>
            <Channel><Variable name="channel"/></Channel>
            <Connection>
              <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],visual_key</ConfigKey>
            </Connection>
            <Connection>
              <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],key_shifted</ConfigKey>
              <BindProperty>highlight</BindProperty>
            </Connection>
          </Key>
          <NumberBpm>
            <ObjectName>DeckStripBpm</ObjectName>
            <TooltipId>visual_bpm</TooltipId>
            <Size>54max,24f</Size>
            <NumberOfDigits>1</NumberOfDigits>
            <Channel><Variable name="channel"/></Channel>
            <Connection>
              <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],visual_bpm</ConfigKey>
            </Connection>
            <Connection>
              <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],rate_ratio</ConfigKey>
              <Transform>
                <IsEqual>1</IsEqual>
                <Not/>
              </Transform>
              <BindProperty>highlight</BindProperty>
            </Connection>
          </NumberBpm>
          <!-- One press both selects the deck and opens the drawer, because
               the trigger CO is what cuepanel.xml's WidgetStack keys on. -->
          <PushButton>
            <ObjectName>DeckStripCueChip</ObjectName>
            <Size>44f,24f</Size>
            <NumberStates>2</NumberStates>
            <State>
              <Number>0</Number>
              <Text>Cue</Text>
            </State>
            <State>
              <Number>1</Number>
              <Text>Cue</Text>
            </State>
            <LeftClickIsPushButton>true</LeftClickIsPushButton>
            <Connection>
              <ConfigKey>[Skin],cue_deck<Variable name="channel"/></ConfigKey>
              <EmitOnDownPress>true</EmitOnDownPress>
            </Connection>
          </PushButton>

          <!-- Eject, two-tap. Two buttons share one slot and swap on
               [Skin],eject_arm<channel>: exactly one is ever visible, and a
               hidden widget takes no width, so the header does not shift when
               it arms. The first tap only sets that control; nothing reaches
               the engine until the second tap on the red one.

               Why not a WidgetStack, which is what sampler.xml uses for the
               same gesture: its page control lives in a currentpage=
               attribute, and SkinContext does not expand <Variable> inside
               attributes (skincontext.h, selectAttributeString reads
               element.attribute() raw). A per-deck template cannot name a
               per-deck control there. The visible swap is the same idiom
               templates/cue_deck_page.xml uses for its two cue banks.

               The armed page fires stop before eject, in document order,
               because BaseTrackPlayerImpl::slotEjectTrack returns early while
               [ChannelN],play is 1 and never stops the deck itself. Drop the
               stop and ejecting a playing deck does nothing at all, with no
               warning and no log line. Same pattern and same reason as
               sampler.xml's UNLOAD button.

               No enabled/track_loaded guard is needed here, unlike the
               sampler's: the whole strip is bound to track_loaded at the foot
               of this file, so an empty deck has no chip to tap and cannot
               reach Mixxx's eject-on-empty "reload the last ejected track"
               gesture.

               There is no timeout. Skin XML has no timer, and a Connection
               can only write widget properties, never controls, so nothing in
               a skin can disarm this on a track load either. An armed chip
               stays red until it is tapped. That is a state you can see,
               rather than a hidden one. -->
          <PushButton>
            <ObjectName>DeckStripEjectChip</ObjectName>
            <Size>44f,24f</Size>
            <NumberStates>1</NumberStates>
            <State>
              <Number>0</Number>
              <Text>EJ</Text>
            </State>
            <Connection>
              <ConfigKey>[Skin],eject_arm<Variable name="channel"/></ConfigKey>
              <ConnectValueToWidget>false</ConnectValueToWidget>
              <EmitOnDownPress>true</EmitOnDownPress>
              <Transform>
                <IsEqual>1</IsEqual>
              </Transform>
            </Connection>
            <Connection>
              <ConnectValueFromWidget>false</ConnectValueFromWidget>
              <ConfigKey>[Skin],eject_arm<Variable name="channel"/></ConfigKey>
              <BindProperty>visible</BindProperty>
              <Transform>
                <Not/>
              </Transform>
            </Connection>
          </PushButton>

          <PushButton>
            <ObjectName>DeckStripEjectChipArmed</ObjectName>
            <Size>44f,24f</Size>
            <NumberStates>1</NumberStates>
            <State>
              <Number>0</Number>
              <Text>EJECT</Text>
            </State>
            <Connection>
              <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],stop</ConfigKey>
              <ConnectValueToWidget>false</ConnectValueToWidget>
              <EmitOnDownPress>true</EmitOnDownPress>
            </Connection>
            <Connection>
              <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],eject</ConfigKey>
              <ConnectValueToWidget>false</ConnectValueToWidget>
              <EmitOnDownPress>true</EmitOnDownPress>
            </Connection>
            <Connection>
              <ConfigKey>[Skin],eject_arm<Variable name="channel"/></ConfigKey>
              <ConnectValueToWidget>false</ConnectValueToWidget>
              <EmitOnDownPress>true</EmitOnDownPress>
              <Transform>
                <IsEqual>0</IsEqual>
              </Transform>
            </Connection>
            <Connection>
              <ConnectValueFromWidget>false</ConnectValueFromWidget>
              <ConfigKey>[Skin],eject_arm<Variable name="channel"/></ConfigKey>
              <BindProperty>visible</BindProperty>
            </Connection>
          </PushButton>
        </Children>
      </WidgetGroup>

      <TrackProperty>
        <ObjectName>DeckStripTitle</ObjectName>
        <TooltipId>track_title</TooltipId>
        <Size>0me,20f</Size>
        <Property>title</Property>
        <Elide>right</Elide>
        <Channel><Variable name="channel"/></Channel>
      </TrackProperty>

      <TrackProperty>
        <ObjectName>DeckStripArtist</ObjectName>
        <TooltipId>track_artist</TooltipId>
        <Size>0me,16f</Size>
        <Property>artist</Property>
        <Elide>right</Elide>
        <Channel><Variable name="channel"/></Channel>
      </TrackProperty>

      <NumberPos>
        <ObjectName>DeckStripTime</ObjectName>
        <TooltipId>track_time</TooltipId>
        <Size>0me,22f</Size>
        <NumberOfDigits>6</NumberOfDigits>
        <Channel><Variable name="channel"/></Channel>
        <Connection>
          <ConfigKey>[Controls],ShowDurationRemaining</ConfigKey>
          <Transform>
            <IsEqual>2</IsEqual>
          </Transform>
          <BindProperty>highlight</BindProperty>
        </Connection>
      </NumberPos>

      <WidgetGroup>
        <ObjectName>DeckStripOverviewContainer</ObjectName>
        <Layout>vertical</Layout>
        <Size>0me,34f</Size>
        <Children>
          <Overview>
            <ObjectName>DeckStripOverview</ObjectName>
            <Size>0me,34f</Size>
            <Channel><Variable name="channel"/></Channel>
            <BgColor>#000</BgColor>
            <SignalColor>#222</SignalColor>
            <SignalLowColor>#007de1</SignalLowColor>
            <SignalMidColor>#007de1</SignalMidColor>
            <SignalHighColor>#007de1</SignalHighColor>
            <PlayedOverlayColor>#40ffffff</PlayedOverlayColor>
            <!-- Time left in the track, drawn straight onto the summary as a
                 watermark: centred and translucent enough to read the signal
                 through. Container and widget are both 0me,34f now — the
                 strip shows the whole overview, not the top half of a
                 double-height one the way deck.xml's did, so the scale is
                 simply a share of the widget's own height, no crop to work
                 around. Every page carries the same strip now, so the
                 watermark is always on; there is no per-tab binding to turn
                 it off on the Play page the way deck.xml had. -->
            <TimeRemainingAlign>center</TimeRemainingAlign>
            <TimeRemainingColor>#fff</TimeRemainingColor>
            <TimeRemainingOpacity>0.55</TimeRemainingOpacity>
            <TimeRemainingScale>0.57</TimeRemainingScale>
            <Mark>
              <Control>cue_point</Control>
              <Color>#eb870f</Color>
            </Mark>
            <!-- Hot cue bank (slots 1-8 = rekordbox pads A-H, and the eight
                 pads a controller maps). Declaring <Hotcue> rather than a
                 position control binds the end position and type too, so a
                 saved loop draws its range and the mark takes the cue's own
                 colour and label; <Color> is only the fallback until a cue
                 exists. -->
            <Mark>
              <Hotcue>1</Hotcue>
              <Text>A</Text>
              <Color>#f44040</Color>
              <TextColor>#f44040</TextColor>
              <Align>top</Align>
            </Mark>
            <Mark>
              <Hotcue>2</Hotcue>
              <Text>B</Text>
              <Color>#0ddcf2</Color>
              <TextColor>#0ddcf2</TextColor>
              <Align>top</Align>
            </Mark>
            <Mark>
              <Hotcue>3</Hotcue>
              <Text>C</Text>
              <Color>#a5df13</Color>
              <TextColor>#a5df13</TextColor>
              <Align>top</Align>
            </Mark>
            <Mark>
              <Hotcue>4</Hotcue>
              <Text>D</Text>
              <Color>#9d4cfd</Color>
              <TextColor>#9d4cfd</TextColor>
              <Align>top</Align>
            </Mark>
            <Mark>
              <Hotcue>5</Hotcue>
              <Text>E</Text>
              <Color>#3fec2b</Color>
              <TextColor>#3fec2b</TextColor>
              <Align>top</Align>
            </Mark>
            <Mark>
              <Hotcue>6</Hotcue>
              <Text>F</Text>
              <Color>#e6681c</Color>
              <TextColor>#e6681c</TextColor>
              <Align>top</Align>
            </Mark>
            <Mark>
              <Hotcue>7</Hotcue>
              <Text>G</Text>
              <Color>#2749c8</Color>
              <TextColor>#2749c8</TextColor>
              <Align>top</Align>
            </Mark>
            <Mark>
              <Hotcue>8</Hotcue>
              <Text>H</Text>
              <Color>#c7b205</Color>
              <TextColor>#c7b205</TextColor>
              <Align>top</Align>
            </Mark>
            <!-- Memory cue bank (slots 17-24, chronological). Bottom-aligned
                 so a glance separates them from the hot cues on top; they sit
                 alongside CUE, which is memory cue 1. Keep in step with
                 kMemoryCueBankStart / kMemoryCueBankSize in cueinfo.h. -->
            <Mark>
              <Hotcue>17</Hotcue>
              <Text>M1</Text>
              <Color>#9aa0a6</Color>
              <TextColor>#9aa0a6</TextColor>
              <Align>bottom</Align>
            </Mark>
            <Mark>
              <Hotcue>18</Hotcue>
              <Text>M2</Text>
              <Color>#9aa0a6</Color>
              <TextColor>#9aa0a6</TextColor>
              <Align>bottom</Align>
            </Mark>
            <Mark>
              <Hotcue>19</Hotcue>
              <Text>M3</Text>
              <Color>#9aa0a6</Color>
              <TextColor>#9aa0a6</TextColor>
              <Align>bottom</Align>
            </Mark>
            <Mark>
              <Hotcue>20</Hotcue>
              <Text>M4</Text>
              <Color>#9aa0a6</Color>
              <TextColor>#9aa0a6</TextColor>
              <Align>bottom</Align>
            </Mark>
            <Mark>
              <Hotcue>21</Hotcue>
              <Text>M5</Text>
              <Color>#9aa0a6</Color>
              <TextColor>#9aa0a6</TextColor>
              <Align>bottom</Align>
            </Mark>
            <Mark>
              <Hotcue>22</Hotcue>
              <Text>M6</Text>
              <Color>#9aa0a6</Color>
              <TextColor>#9aa0a6</TextColor>
              <Align>bottom</Align>
            </Mark>
            <Mark>
              <Hotcue>23</Hotcue>
              <Text>M7</Text>
              <Color>#9aa0a6</Color>
              <TextColor>#9aa0a6</TextColor>
              <Align>bottom</Align>
            </Mark>
            <Mark>
              <Hotcue>24</Hotcue>
              <Text>M8</Text>
              <Color>#9aa0a6</Color>
              <TextColor>#9aa0a6</TextColor>
              <Align>bottom</Align>
            </Mark>
            <Mark>
              <Control>loop_start_position</Control>
              <Color>#6ee128</Color>
            </Mark>
            <Mark>
              <Control>loop_end_position</Control>
              <Color>#6ee128</Color>
            </Mark>
            <MarkRange>
              <StartControl>loop_start_position</StartControl>
              <EndControl>loop_end_position</EndControl>
              <EnabledControl>loop_enabled</EnabledControl>
              <Color>#6ee128</Color>
              <Opacity>0.8</Opacity>
              <DisabledColor>#acacac</DisabledColor>
              <DisabledOpacity>0.4</DisabledOpacity>
            </MarkRange>
            <Connection>
              <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],playposition</ConfigKey>
            </Connection>
          </Overview>
        </Children>
      </WidgetGroup>

    </Children>
    <Connection>
      <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],track_loaded</ConfigKey>
      <BindProperty>visible</BindProperty>
    </Connection>
  </WidgetGroup>
</Template>
